# Core rules

- Read `PRD.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and the relevant ADR before changing architecture.
- The consumer system is Android-first, phone-only, offline-first, and emits navigation at 10 Hz.
- No OBD-II, vehicle speedometer, cloud inference, LiDAR, or custom vehicle hardware dependency.
- Keep raw sensor timestamps as integer nanoseconds and document every unit and coordinate frame.
- Algorithms in the live path are causal. Future-aware smoothing is evaluation-only and labeled.
- Hidden ground-truth GNSS is score-only during a blackout. It must not influence features, alignment, model, filter, map hypotheses, or recovery before it becomes available.
- Use explicit status/result types for missing or invalid data. Never convert failures into zeros silently.
- Preserve deterministic replay. Any randomness requires a recorded seed.
- Add tests for numerical limits, timing gaps, transitions, and fallbacks.
- Never invent benchmark values, logs, screenshots, dataset fields, or citations.
- User-facing estimates include confidence and a reason for degradation.
- Keep the project functional without TimesFM and without a learned checkpoint.
- Follow `code-quality.mdc` on every change. Delete dead code instead of leaving it for later.
- Follow `design-anti-vibecode.mdc` for any user-visible surface, including judge mode.

